    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p21-q22-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find all three-digit palindromes divisible by 9.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$171, 252, 333, 414, 585, 666, 747, 828, 909, 999$.\n\nFor digits $a,b$, test whether $2a+b$ is divisible by 9.",
          "worked": "Write the palindrome as $\\overline{aba}$, where $1\\leq a\\leq9$ and $0\\leq b\\leq9$. Its digit sum is $2a+b$, so this must be $9$, $18$ or $27$.\n\nFor digit sum $9$, the possibilities are $171,252,333,414$. For digit sum $18$, they are $585,666,747,828,909$. For digit sum $27$, the only possibility is $999$.\n\nThus all the numbers are $171,252,333,414,585,666,747,828,909,999$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q22-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find all four-digit palindromes divisible by 3 and 5.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$5115,5445,5775$.\n\nDivisibility by 5 fixes the outside digits as 5; test the digit sum for divisibility by 3.",
          "worked": "A four-digit palindrome has the form $\\overline{abba}$. Divisibility by 5 requires the last digit to be $0$ or $5$. The first digit cannot be $0$, so $a=5$.\n\nThe digit sum is $10+2b$. For $b=0,1,\\ldots,9$, this is divisible by 3 exactly when $b=1,4,7$.\n\nThe numbers are $5115,5445,5775$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q22-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Find the smallest five-digit palindrome divisible by 4.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$21012$.\n\nChoose the smallest outside digits that make the final two digits divisible by 4.",
          "worked": "Write the palindrome as $\\overline{abcba}$. Divisibility by 4 depends on its final two digits, $\\overline{ba}$.\n\nThe last digit must be even, so the smallest possible nonzero outside digit is $a=2$. The ending $02$ is not divisible by 4, but $12$ is, so the smallest possible next digit is $b=1$.\n\nChoose the smallest middle digit, $c=0$. The smallest number is $21012$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q22-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Find the largest five-digit palindrome divisible by 5.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$59995$.",
          "worked": "Divisibility by 5 requires a final digit of $0$ or $5$. In a five-digit palindrome the first and last digits are equal, so both must be $5$.\n\nMaximise the three remaining digits by making each $9$. The largest number is $59995$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q22-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "Find the largest five-digit palindrome divisible by 4.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$88988$.\n\nMaximise the leading digits while keeping the final two digits divisible by 4.",
          "worked": "Write the palindrome as $\\overline{abcba}$. A multiple of 4 is even, so the largest possible outside digit is $a=8$.\n\nThe ending $98$ is not divisible by 4, but $88$ is, so the largest possible next digit is $b=8$.\n\nChoose the largest middle digit, $c=9$. The largest number is $88988$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q22-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "Find the smallest five-digit palindrome divisible by 4 and 9.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$21312$.\n\nThe smallest possible outside pairs give $21c12$; divisibility by 9 then requires $c=3$.",
          "worked": "Write the palindrome as $\\overline{abcba}$. Divisibility by 4 requires an even last digit. The smallest possible outside digit is $a=2$, and the smallest next digit giving an ending divisible by 4 is $b=1$.\n\nThe number therefore has the form $21c12$. Its digit sum is $6+c$, which must be divisible by 9.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}6+c&=9\\\\c&=3\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe smallest number is $21312$. Its final two digits are $12$ and its digit sum is $9$, so it satisfies both tests.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 76
      }
    ]
  },
